{"title":"1998 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO\" title=\"1998 USAMO\"> 1998</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"USAMO\">USAMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose that the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f72854961d8a9472daefd47b0b089867605b429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,\\cdots, 1998\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> has been partitioned into disjoint pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00f64870b76e16d812d79938c0f7bd59426e8c2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_i,b_i\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b836c8edc0bdd0fcc8467756a26406902d1657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i\\leq 999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />) so that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b88963fc9f7c4fa923c59d185083d05b54103cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_i-b_i|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the sum\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/8/c986d59da1a579f6d783633ebe60315bc9ede782.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a_1-b_1|+|a_2-b_2|+\\cdots +|a_{999}-b_{999}|\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"18\" />\nends in the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23bff7d9649b742e2a9d22cfce5c3eb891697184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b1bb8663e4a744dc1c459290af22a3b3eaae05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> be  concentric circles, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b1bb8663e4a744dc1c459290af22a3b3eaae05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> in the interior of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23bff7d9649b742e2a9d22cfce5c3eb891697184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. From a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23bff7d9649b742e2a9d22cfce5c3eb891697184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> one draws the tangent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b1bb8663e4a744dc1c459290af22a3b3eaae05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c5d1bf526c8d98272f4a3fd8df629570bd0c6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B\\in {\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the second point of intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23bff7d9649b742e2a9d22cfce5c3eb891697184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. A line passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b1bb8663e4a744dc1c459290af22a3b3eaae05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in such a way that the perpendicular  bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> intersect at a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Find, with proof,  the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83531a4c13b687601c8e55f86b2bf7412fe1db9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM/MC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41f73167171b96584a6f3326ff5af6f73859c896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0,a_1,\\cdots ,a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> be numbers from the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea2852b1107f65493606cdb65bb24f53f657ccbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,\\pi/2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a17a13ad73967fad48014bf548f0d687fa1f5c3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan \\left(a_0-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+ \\tan \\left(a_1-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+\\cdots +\\tan \\left(a_n-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\geq n-1.\\]\" width=\"473\" height=\"33\" />\nProve that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff4e13e0ea9edf3911192881d1fb2e4bfabf76d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan a_0\\tan a_1 \\cdots \\tan a_n\\geq n^{n+1}.\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"18\" />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A computer screen shows a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80aff5434bbe62da6bbadc989c93c1ea4e3dc0f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98 \\times 98$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> chessboard, colored in the usual way. One can select with a mouse any rectangle with sides on the lines of the chessboard and click the mouse button: as a result,  the colors in the selected rectangle switch (black becomes white, white becomes black). Find, with proof, the minimum number of mouse clicks needed to make the chessboard all one color.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47affecc93688552c8eca8bc13560d52b4cc28a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, there is a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a65fe5f396d8c182d88144d00e26156435e0743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> for every distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bda82ee8212aa2c03bc02d76fc28a5bda8412ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47f57bec2b79615225569e1ab7a59d042a73c48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> be an integer. Find the largest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> (as a function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />) such that there exists a convex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a3f6f060f4e08fc2ccdde66d1a631e08e127d36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{1}A_{2}\\dots A_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> for which exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> of the quadrilaterals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633732a84607043d204feace8f8ee547673d6ac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{i}A_{i+1}A_{i+2}A_{i+3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"17\" /> have an inscribed circle. (Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c739175a820ab8d5eeafa0d4c802d22ffafb9ae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n+j} = A_{j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" />.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO\" title=\"1998 USAMO\">1998 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO\" title=\"1997 USAMO\">1997 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO\" title=\"1999 USAMO\">1999 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017200816\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.068 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 319/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1255/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 64/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9092/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   25.932      1 -total\n 73.65%   19.100      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 24.87%    6.448 